1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,197
Pretty notes that never become action are a hobby.

2
00:00:03,197 --> 00:00:05,683
This lesson is about note-taking that ships.

3
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:07,104
Capture next actions only.

4
00:00:07,104 --> 00:00:09,590
Do not treat this as theory only.

5
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:13,142
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

6
00:00:13,142 --> 00:00:18,470
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

7
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:22,378
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

8
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:26,640
Stay practical: create a next-action note before you optimize branding or tools.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,492
Capture next actions only.

10
00:00:28,492 --> 00:00:29,258
One sentence.

11
00:00:29,258 --> 00:00:30,025
Verb first.

12
00:00:30,025 --> 00:00:31,940
Owner and deadline if needed.

13
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:34,621
Remember the objective: create a next-action note.

14
00:00:34,621 --> 00:00:38,835
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

15
00:00:38,835 --> 00:00:43,432
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

16
00:00:43,432 --> 00:00:47,646
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

17
00:00:47,646 --> 00:00:52,242
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

18
00:00:52,242 --> 00:00:54,924
Talk to a real person when possible.

19
00:00:54,924 --> 00:00:56,456
Feedback beats guessing alone.

20
00:00:56,776 --> 00:01:01,557
Drop quotes, highlights, and theory dumps unless they change what you do tomorrow.

